Abstract = {Experimentally it is found that the pressure dependence of T-c, in
   high-T-c superconductors, is influenced by several factors. The carrier
   density, the doping, and the contraction of the unit cell are some of
   these factors. This contraction may change the 2D character of some
   cuprate superconductors. In this work, 2D and quasi-2D models, with
   energy band overlap, are used to describe cuprate superconductors under
   pressure. The results for Y124 are reported. (C) 2004 Elsevier B.V. All
   rights reserved.},
