Month = {JAN},
Abstract = {The present study deals with the changes in the larval fish community
   structure off the west coast of Baja California resulting from the
   relaxation of the environmental changes induced by the 1983 El Nino
   event up to August 1985. Larval fish assemblages defined two sampling
   station clusters, as could be determined from the corresponding
   dendrograms. Their distribution pattern was primarily influenced by
   spawning area selection, but seasonal and interannual changes which
   appeared to be related with the ocean dynamics during El Nino events,
   were also important.},
